.TH "AUTOSNAP" "1" "Aug 2026" "autosnap" "autosnap manual"

.SH NAME
autosnap-branch - Create Git branches with autosnap checkpoints


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBautosnap branch [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create Git branches and copy autosnap checkpoint refs between branch namespaces.

.PP
Autosnap checkpoints are stored as refs under refs/autosnapshots//.
Branch commands copy those refs. They do not duplicate checkpoint commit
objects, apply checkpoint patches, or push anything to a remote.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for branch


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBautosnap(1)\fP, \fBautosnap-branch-copy(1)\fP, \fBautosnap-branch-create(1)\fP
